hMailServer for Debian
======================

This package is built without the server's live update: apt updates it. The
server still checks for a newer release, when its update check is on, and
names the command that installs it: apt upgrade hmailserver.

It is installed enabled and stopped. Before it can start it needs a database
(PostgreSQL, or MySQL and MariaDB with libmariadb3), an administrator password
and a schema; /usr/share/doc/hmailserver/README.md, "Install and get running",
has every step, in short:

  sudoedit /etc/hmailserver/hMailServer.ini           [Database]
  sudo hmailserver --set-admin-password
  sudo -u hmailserver hmailserver --create-database
  sudo hmailserver --create-stored-secrets-key
  sudo hmailserver --export-stored-secrets-key /root/hmailserver-stored-secrets.key
  sudo -u hmailserver hmailserver --check-config
  sudo systemctl start hmailserver

The REST API, the Control Deck in a browser and hmctl (the hmailserver-cli
package) need the REST listener, which is off: sudo hmailserver --set-setting
RestApiPort=8080, then restart the service.

Purging the package removes its configuration and /var/log/hmailserver. It
leaves the mail store, /var/lib/hmailserver, the database and the hmailserver
account: remove those by hand once you are sure.

